# Component filenames

When creating or editing React components under `app/components/`:

- Use **PascalCase** for component filenames (e.g. `PasskeyManager.tsx`, `Greeting.tsx`)
- Subdirectories (`auth/`, `account/`) stay lowercase — only the `.tsx`/`.jsx` basename is PascalCase
- Import paths must match the filename (e.g. `@/app/components/auth/PasskeyManager`)

## Good

- `PasskeySignInForm.tsx`
- `SignOutButton.tsx`
- `Greeting.tsx`

## Bad

- `passkey-sign-in-form.tsx`
- `sign-out-button.tsx`
- `greeting.tsx`

When renaming components, use `git mv`. On macOS, use a two-step rename for case-only changes (e.g. `greeting.tsx` → `Greeting.tmp.tsx` → `Greeting.tsx`) and update all import sites.
